# Login Fix Verification

I have fixed the issue where the admin user creation and login were failing due to missing and mismatched password hashing logic.

## Changes Made
- **Centralized Security Logic**: Moved [get_password_hash](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py#10-12) and [verify_password](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py#7-9) to [backend/utils/security.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/utils/security.py).
- **Fixed User Creation**: Updated [backend/crud/user.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/crud/user.py) to correctly import security functions.
- **Removed Invalid Fields**: Removed `name`, `surname`, and `nickname` from initialization logic as they are not present in the current database model.
- **Fixed Docker Imports**: Updated [init_admin.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/init_admin.py) to use relative/module-level imports compatible with the Docker environment.

